---
title: Tofu Bacon Bits
servings: 4
tags: vegan, plant-based, bacon, tofu, condiment
source: https://shakaylafelice.substack.com/p/tomato-sandwich-with-a-tofu-bacon
---

In a bowl, combine all the marinade ingredients: @soy sauce{1/3%cup}, @Worcestershire sauce{1%tbsp}, @liquid smoke{2%tsp}, @tomato paste{2%tsp}, @maple syrup{2%tsp}, @nutritional yeast{1%tbsp}, @garlic powder{1.5%tsp}, @onion powder{1.5%tsp}, @smoked paprika{1/2%tsp}, and @water{1/4%cup}. Whisk until well incorporated.

Thinly slice the @tofu{1%block}(super firm, or fava bean tofu for soy-free) into bacon-like strips. Transfer the tofu to the marinade and gently break apart into smaller, bacon bit-sized pieces. Cover and let marinate for at least ~marinate{30%minutes}.

Preheat the #oven to 370°F. Spread the marinated tofu and marinade in a single layer onto a large, greased baking sheet using @spray olive oil{}. If your baking sheet is small, cook in batches.

Bake for ~bake{75%minutes}, flipping the tofu at 30 minute intervals, until crispy. Keep a close eye to prevent burning. Let cool completely before using.

> Makes several servings — feel free to use the remaining tofu bacon
